`lastIndex` was computed once before the deletion loop, causing incorrect trailing blank row detection after earlier items were deleted and indices shifted.

### Changes
- Replace static index comparison with dynamic check that identifies trailing blank row by its properties:
  - Empty text content
  - Current last position in list

```cpp
// Before: stale index comparison
const long lastIndex = GetItemCount() - 1;
if (item == lastIndex) { continue; }

// After: dynamic check
if (GetItemText(item).IsEmpty() && item == GetItemCount() - 1) { continue; }
```

