Build a web-based roulette game that randomly selects one name from a user-provided list.

## Implementation

Single self-contained `index.html` with embedded CSS/JavaScript:

- **Name management**: Add/remove names with validation (no empty/duplicate entries)
- **Roulette animation**: 3-second CSS spin (1800deg rotation) with randomized name display during animation
- **Winner selection**: Random pick from list, displayed in wheel center with golden announcement banner
- **UI/UX**: Responsive gradient design, Indonesian language, disabled states during spinning

## Technical Details

```javascript
// Core roulette logic
function startRoulette() {
    // Rapid name cycling during 3s animation
    spinInterval = setInterval(() => {
        const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * names.length);
        rouletteContent.textContent = names[randomIndex];
    }, 100);

    // Final winner selection after animation
    setTimeout(() => {
        const winner = names[Math.floor(Math.random() * names.length)];
        displayWinner(winner);
    }, 3000);
}
```

Zero dependencies, pure vanilla JavaScript, works in any modern browser.

