Implements three UX improvements: consistent button widths across position/precision toggles, single-click handle display for touch devices, and clickable legend/panel headers for box interaction.

## Changes

### Unified Button Widths
- Position toggles (Initial/Final): `120px` min-width
- Drag precision buttons: `68px` min-width  
- Load sample button: `120px` min-width
- All buttons center-aligned for visual consistency

### Single-Click Handle Display
- Added `AppState.handlesVisibleForBox` state to track handle visibility independent of box activation
- Modified `BoxPreviewCanvas.drawBox()` to show handles when `handlesVisibleForBox` matches box index
- Single click on canvas box or UI elements shows corner/edge handles; click elsewhere hides them
- Consolidates multiple `redraw()` calls into single invocation

### Legend & Panel Header Interaction
- Added `data-box` attributes to legend items for explicit index mapping
- Extracted common logic into `showHandlesForBox()` and `toggleBoxActivation()` methods
- Single click shows handles, double click activates/locks box
- Validation prevents NaN box indices with console warnings

## Code Example

```javascript
// Before: Hover required to see handles (desktop), no quick access on mobile
// After: Single click shows handles immediately
onClick(e) {
    const hitInfo = this.hitTest(pos.x, pos.y);
    if (hitInfo) {
        AppState.handlesVisibleForBox = hitInfo.boxIndex;
        this.redraw();
    } else {
        // Consolidated redraw
        let needsRedraw = false;
        if (AppState.handlesVisibleForBox !== null) {
            AppState.handlesVisibleForBox = null;
            needsRedraw = true;
        }
        if (needsRedraw) this.redraw();
    }
}
```

